<%= example('local-device-unavailable') %>

## Use the right state

| Situation | Say | Do not say |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The request succeeded and there are no warnings | No current warnings | Unavailable |
| The entity has not given a usable state | Reading unknown | 0 or Off |
| The entity reports `unavailable` | Reading unavailable | Definitely offline |
| Only an earlier observation exists | Last reported value, with its date and time | A new reading |
| Home Assistant rejected the request | Request rejected, with the known reason | The device did not respond |
| The request was accepted but no new state has arrived | Request accepted; result not confirmed | Failed, succeeded or safe to repeat |
| The Civica colour controls are disabled because not every Civica theme is installed | Install all Civica themes and reload themes to use these controls. | Leaving the controls disabled without a reason |
| A chosen Civica theme is absent when the person applies it | This theme is unavailable. Reload themes and try again. | A silent switch to another theme colour |
| Home Assistant has not yet supplied its themes | Colour settings are loading. | An error |
| Home Assistant is in safe or recovery mode | Colour controls are unavailable in safe or recovery mode. | Hiding the native theme settings |
| The profile controls cannot attach | Use the native theme selector or the settings card | Hiding the native settings |

## Keep the person’s context

Keep what they entered, and name the device or setting. Put the message next to the control it concerns. Keep recovery steps short and specific. Offer Retry only when it really retries.

## Do not interrupt repeatedly

Do not announce every sensor refresh. Leave a lasting unavailable state visible without raising a new alert each time the dashboard updates. Respect reduced motion and do not flash warnings.

## Collect useful diagnostics

For a bug report, record the Home Assistant version, browser version, selected theme, affected component and steps to reproduce. Leave credentials, tokens, addresses and private device details out of screenshots and logs unless the person chooses to share them.

For the shared status labels, see [Status and notifications](../components/status.html). For the wording rules, see [States, requests and errors](../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html).

## Test the failure, not only the success

Start from the current confirmed state. Reach every action by keyboard and check its label names the affected object. Check pending, failed and unavailable results, and never replace missing data with zero. Repeat at narrow width and larger text.

A preview proves only how the pattern looks. The connected application must separately prove permissions, native routing, state confirmation and recovery.
